    "gold_precision": 0.2,
    "refused": false,
    "answer": "An insert-only table is useful when the application needs access to history, such as in a banking application designed to present customer address history [Ch. 5]. It can also be beneficial in maintaining a current view of data, where new versions of records are inserted without deleting old records, and a query or view can present the current data state by finding the newest record by primary key [Ch. 8]. Additionally, insert-only tables can be used in the enhanced Lambda architecture used by BigQuery and Apache Druid, where deletes and in-place updates can still be expensive [Ch. 8].",
